emy-id "q-20061" :question/problem "Find $c\\cdot (b\\times a)$, if $3a\\cdot (6b\\times c)=90.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a\\cdot (6b\\times c) & =90 \\\\ 3\\cdot 6\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =90 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a) & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-20061/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e0b4d33-7699-5068-90f1-663534cd662d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20061"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73462/selection/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" :answer/id #uuid "7d50ad68-816f-572e-8949-8d9d589d732c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73462/selection/5d34995cddd0166b343cae457ee45643c04c739e08758db1204c66c5ee04158e" :answer/id #uuid "d48bfb0b-5827-5081-8b15-f6364120b40d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73462/selection/906fb68e52f34c93aaa89471be2f2ff4994dc9adb32c934377257fa64a54e307" :answer/id #uuid "5003ffc7-63f1-5367-b3ad-3f386ee6bc7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73462/selection/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708" :answer/id #uuid "c17e8fa2-7bef-5bff-b3fc-776b1483bc5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73462/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "03cbecf2-35d0-52fc-8bac-82478409f037" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73462/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f54c99f4-44c8-58cb-ade9-1afcce4aae47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73462/selection/906fb68e52f34c93aaa89471be2f2ff4994dc9adb32c934377257fa64a54e307" :answer-field/choices ["q-73462/selection/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" "q-73462/selection/5d34995cddd0166b343cae457ee45643c04c739e08758db1204c66c5ee04158e" "q-73462/selection/906fb68e52f34c93aaa89471be2f2ff4994dc9adb32c934377257fa64a54e307" "q-73462/selection/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708" "q-73462/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73462" :question/id #uuid "56a67151-433c-536b-a8d9-272b277f7ee7" :question/math-academy-id "q-73462" :question/problem "Let $p=⟨3,1,2⟩$, $q=⟨1,-2,1⟩$ and $r=⟨4,1,-2⟩.$ Find $r\\cdot (q\\times p).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $r\\cdot (q\\times p)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $r,$ $q,$ and $p.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot (q\\times p) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4((-2)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-(1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3)-2(1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-20+1-14 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73462/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff317cd2-0896-5134-b3a3-4e9f84e22b68"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73462"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128356/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "0f71b61f-e092-559d-8d6a-4cf84c4dedca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128356/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "66b11125-8799-5340-9fe2-95167706219c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128356/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "800b5064-612d-577c-89cc-7f0b2ee0cc3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128356/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "fca2c88f-dea8-5a26-8ae1-9c6fc3d3bb99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128356/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "1d11cbd0-3e23-5364-b5f8-b77b7c5fab0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128356/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ed33f73-a6f0-58c5-b6b8-57e78ea67208" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128356/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-128356/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-128356/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-128356/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-128356/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-128356/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128356" :question/id #uuid "f1104b66-46a9-5ac3-b3cf-8d4361282db9" :question/math-academy-id "q-128356" :question/problem "Find $c\\cdot (b\\times a),$ if $b\\times c=⟨6,-1,3⟩$ and $a=⟨3,5,-4⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨3,5,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =3\\cdot 6+5\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =18-5-12 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-128356/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e0b4d33-7699-5068-90f1-663534cd662d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128356"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317312/field-1/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" :answer/id #uuid "28024be1-e60c-52c4-8be3-e113dd2ae063" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317312/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d5211f76-1319-5e68-9c3c-3c3c02052df9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317312/field-1/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" :answer-field/choices ["q-317312/field-1/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317312" :question/id #uuid "79b88d55-66e2-53f6-b61e-729c93ab168f" :question/math-academy-id "q-317312" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2,-1,3⟩$, $b=⟨0,4,1⟩$ and $c=⟨-2,1,5⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\,(4\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 1)\\,-\\,(-1)\\,(0\\cdot 5-1\\cdot (-2))\\,+\\,3\\,(0\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =2\\,(19)\\,-\\,(-1)\\,(2)\\,+\\,3\\,(8) \\\\  & =38+2+24 \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-317312/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff317cd2-0896-5134-b3a3-4e9f84e22b68"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317312"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317316/field-1/ac46572169135c39bc2dc1bfb75349ed12f60a1187a3ef59cacec084b49d12ff" :answer/id #uuid "0e25707d-29d4-5b02-a14f-55bfafd7aae3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317316/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "035c26d1-e476-54e3-81a9-2efec90d74f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317316/field-1/ac46572169135c39bc2dc1bfb75349ed12f60a1187a3ef59cacec084b49d12ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-317316/field-1/ac46572169135c39bc2dc1bfb75349ed12f60a1187a3ef59cacec084b49d12ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317316" :question/id #uuid "4d5ac22a-d2ea-5551-a038-9b2a5e99fb58" :question/math-academy-id "q-317316" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨0,2,5⟩$, $b=⟨3,1,0⟩$ and $c=⟨4,-1,-2⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\,(1\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot (-1))\\,-\\,2\\,(3\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 4)\\,+\\,5\\,(3\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =0(-2)\\,-\\,2\\,(-6)\\,+\\,5\\,(-7) \\\\  & =0+12-35 \\\\  & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-317316/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff317cd2-0896-5134-b3a3-4e9f84e22b68"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317316"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
